{"connection_id": "BC-fdbe4ba5a0d410e9848b", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.14.6", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "Jesus identifies himself as the way", "note": "Where the source has a community ask God to guide it on a straight path, John identifies Jesus himself as the way to the Father; the contrast is a substantive Christological recasting of path language."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f464b423e66df8391a10", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.15.5", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "apart from me you can do nothing", "note": "Branches can bear fruit only by remaining in the vine, and apart from Christ disciples can do nothing; it gives the source's inability to proceed alone an organic image of dependence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5d1c1143e51ff68ab348", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.16.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Spirit guides into all truth", "note": "The Spirit of truth guides disciples into all truth; it extends the source's request for a guide from physical route-finding to discernment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c66fcada617db3b84477", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.5.7", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "No one to help him reach the water", "note": "The disabled man says he has no one to put him in the pool and another enters first; his particular inability to move without assistance embodies the commentary's dependent traveler asking for support."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5c7a06f2ff3718245405", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.5.7", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no one to help the disabled man", "note": "The disabled man says he has no person to put him into the pool; this sharpens the commentary's premise that a weak traveler cannot manage alone."}
{"connection_id": "BC-946088737b7ecdb08cad", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.5.8", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Rise and walk", "note": "Jesus tells the man to rise, take his mat, and walk; the command's result is a body restored to upright movement, the outcome pictured in the commentary's supported traveler."}
{"connection_id": "BC-aaa425519e7187cf4013", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.5.8", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rise, take up bed, walk", "note": "Jesus commands the man to rise, carry his bed, and walk; it gives the source's requested help its compact standing-and-road outcome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-125fe1b090bd58ccc2e1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jude.1.24", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Kept from stumbling and presented standing", "note": "The doxology praises God as able to keep believers from stumbling and present them blameless before his glory; it turns the commentary's bodily image of being steadied into a promise about standing securely before God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c4a482832d0479d7f725", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jude.1.24", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "kept from stumbling and made to stand", "note": "God is able to keep believers from stumbling and make them stand; it compresses the source's protected gait and upright result into doxology."}
{"connection_id": "BC-783bb98e2dec2e7ad740", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.1.79", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Feet guided into peace", "note": "In Zechariah's blessing, God will guide the feet of those in darkness into the way of peace; its prayer-like language explicitly joins guidance, feet, and a path as the commentary does."}
{"connection_id": "BC-68e5b7efa7ceb8efea58", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.1.79", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "guide feet into the way of peace", "note": "The dawn from on high guides feet into the way of peace; it closely matches ihdina as guidance enacted at the feet."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a2609b6ba16fbd28f70f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.10.30", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "traveler left half dead on the road", "note": "The traveler falls among robbers and is left half dead; this supplies the vulnerable roadside condition to which the Samaritan's assistance in the existing scene responds."}
{"connection_id": "BC-09c91b282cc373364e6b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.10.34", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A wounded traveler receives support", "note": "The Samaritan binds the wounded man's injuries, puts him on his own animal, and brings him to an inn; the story reverses the commentary's exhausted mount but shares its precise scene of a vulnerable traveler kept moving by another's practical care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c2967e2121767b5be136", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.10.34", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "injured traveler placed on an animal", "note": "The Samaritan binds an injured traveler's wounds, puts him on his own animal, and brings him to care; it reverses the source's failed mount into a means of carrying the weak."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4ab860c4f9a46c4b518a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.10.35", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Care continues after rescue", "note": "The Samaritan pays the innkeeper and promises further expenses for the wounded traveler; this extends the commentary's image of leaning on support into sustained care beyond the first act of getting someone upright."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4441fc74aa9e937cd676", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.13.11", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bent over; unable to straighten", "note": "The woman's disabling spirit leaves her bent and unable to straighten; it supplies an exact counter-image to the upright mustaqim walker."}
{"connection_id": "BC-610764dfbcff37a7ce23", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.13.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The bent woman stands upright", "note": "Jesus lays hands on a woman bent for eighteen years and she immediately stands straight and glorifies God; the scene joins bodily restoration to praise, as the commentary joins uprightness with worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-307a42a8df93928dbf58", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.13.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "made straight after Jesus' touch", "note": "After Jesus lays hands on her, the woman is immediately made straight; the touch makes aid visibly become upright posture."}
