{"connection_id": "BC-2c6942154f852d30ab78", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Prayer for protection and rescue", "note": "The Lord's Prayer asks not to be brought into trial and asks for deliverance from evil; this is a specific communal petition for divine help alongside the commentary's prayer that worshippers cannot proceed alone."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ad715a54d1a05a7cecba", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "communal petition for protection from testing", "note": "The plural prayer asks not to be brought into testing and to be delivered from evil; it forms a Christian liturgical companion to the communal request for guided protection."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a8075e45c7f7bdb55173", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.14", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A difficult way leading to life", "note": "Jesus describes the narrow gate and hard way that lead to life, with few finding them; this makes the requested path a morally consequential course, while the surah's surrounding verse specifies its own blessed and rejected ways."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e39b734434b716281b7e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.25", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "house does not fall because founded on rock", "note": "The house withstands storm because it has a rock foundation; it gives the source's wall and structural support imagery an ethical architectural counterpart."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e97dcd64238acd80738f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.12", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The dead before the throne", "note": "The dead stand before the great throne as books are opened and they are judged by what is written; this supplies a distinct vision of the day of reckoning named in the selected ayah."}
{"connection_id": "BC-33b992ebcdd222be4928", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.7.17", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Lamb shepherds and guides to waters", "note": "The Lamb shepherds the afflicted and guides them to springs of life-giving water; it combines leadership, relief, and a destination for the needy traveler."}
{"connection_id": "BC-da186780e15488341528", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.14.13", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "do not put obstacle in a brother's way", "note": "Believers are told not to put a stumbling block or obstacle in another's way; it turns the source's safe path into a responsibility toward a fellow walker."}
{"connection_id": "BC-503a75f28f1ce2a32b4c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.14.4", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "servant made to stand by the Lord", "note": "The servant stands or falls before the master, yet the Lord is able to make the servant stand; it brings service, dependence, and uprightness into one statement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-100f4eb961a4d96450ca", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.15.1", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The strong bear the weak", "note": "Paul says the strong ought to bear the weaknesses of those without strength rather than please themselves; this turns the commentary's supported walk into a concrete communal obligation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-64eeccb73a714f599393", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.15.1", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "strong bear the weak's frailties", "note": "The strong are obliged to bear the frailties of the weak; it states the communal duty implicit in the commentary's two supporting companions."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e33b44461fc2466ee4f7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.8.26", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The Spirit helps weakness in prayer", "note": "Paul says the Spirit helps believers in their weakness because they do not know how to pray as they ought; this closely links the commentary's inability to proceed alone with its joining worship and a request for help."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cd7d87ab51460f737c1d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.8.26", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Spirit helps weakness in prayer", "note": "The Spirit helps human weakness when people do not know how to pray; it applies requested divine aid to the very act of supplication."}
{"connection_id": "BC-07fdacf989effbe42c09", "ref": "1QS 3:20", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sons of righteousness walk in paths of light", "note": "The Community Rule places the sons of righteousness under the Prince of Lights and says they walk in paths of light; it gives the requested right way an angelic and communal Second Temple framing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-407d5946d8d978b97b90", "ref": "Baruch 5:7", "target": "sec11", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "level ground so Israel walks safely", "note": "God levels mountains and fills valleys so Israel may walk safely; it develops the source's straightened route as a bodily safe passage."}
