+{"connection_id":"BC-066b32579ee64fac2237","ref":"WLC:Ps.107.6","status":"accepted","reason":"The cry for help precedes being led in a straight way, matching the prayer's sequence.","paragraphs":[57],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.107.6","WLC:Ps.107.7"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-005"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f430c8647b45c9bdcbcb","ref":"WLC:Ps.107.7","status":"accepted","reason":"YHWH explicitly leads the rescued group along a straight way to an inhabited city.","paragraphs":[57],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.107.6","WLC:Ps.107.7"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-005"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-81d418d308327f39da27","ref":"WLC:Ps.107.7","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew דרך ישרה names a straight way directly after the group's cry in verse 6.","paragraphs":[57],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.107.6","WLC:Ps.107.7"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-005"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ece76199c7803acd16c9","ref":"WLC:Ps.116.8","status":"rejected","reason":"Feet saved from stumbling form part of a thanksgiving list, but no actual support or straight route is named; Psalm 94:18 adds a slipping foot and aid.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.116.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0043afe76bea94a80f3b","ref":"WLC:Ps.119.133","status":"rejected","reason":"The petitioner asks to establish steps in God's word, but the moral-word context lacks a failing body or helper; Psalm 27:11 is the closer road petition.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.119.133"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-5fb584a4ef702cd5c969","ref":"WLC:Ps.119.35","status":"rejected","reason":"Lead me on the path of commandments is a direct prayer, but Psalm 27:11 also specifies a level way, making it more exact for mustaqim.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.119.35"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-eb05d61dc6e3db7e65a6","ref":"WLC:Ps.121.2","status":"rejected","reason":"The pilgrim's help comes from YHWH, but this verse alone does not connect help to uprightness or a straight path as Psalm 107:6-7 does.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.121.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fa112e20b0d42f578ea9","ref":"WLC:Ps.121.3","status":"rejected","reason":"The statement that help comes from YHWH is in Psalm 121:2, not 121:3; verse 3 concerns the foot's slipping.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.121.3","WLC:Ps.121.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-8baf3da4e76c1ad515d8","ref":"WLC:Ps.121.3","status":"rejected","reason":"God guards the pilgrim's foot from slipping, but Psalm 94:18 adds the speaker's explicit slipping foot and supporting mercy.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.121.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d07cc781114529d88981","ref":"WLC:Ps.123.2","status":"rejected","reason":"Servants watch a master's hand for mercy, but the hand is a sign of authority, not a support holding their bodies upright.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.123.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b70cb0d5f56c2d13f619","ref":"WLC:Ps.145.14","status":"rejected","reason":"YHWH supports the falling and straightens the bowed, close imagery; Isaiah 41:10-13 adds the sought helping hand to the same support point.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.145.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-bdcc53f37a2aa3043939","ref":"WLC:Ps.145.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Falling and straightening occur in Psalm 145:14; verse 15 says all eyes look to God for food.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.145.15","WLC:Ps.145.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-89d1d9375ee19b3f93df","ref":"WLC:Ps.18.34","status":"rejected","reason":"Deerlike feet on heights are part of a royal victory song, not a weakened person's plea for help or a straight road.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.18.34"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1cc8674c8fbc98a31523","ref":"WLC:Ps.18.37","status":"rejected","reason":"Wide steps prevent ankles slipping, but the victory context lacks the direct cry-and-support point of Psalm 94:18.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.18.37"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3ad8b006c2e65466cc50","ref":"WLC:Ps.23.4","status":"rejected","reason":"Leading in paths of righteousness is Psalm 23:3, not 23:4; verse 4 names the dark valley and comforting staff.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.23.4","WLC:Ps.23.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e2525636b56374127945","ref":"WLC:Ps.23.5","status":"rejected","reason":"The staff that comforts in the dark valley is at Psalm 23:4; verse 5 describes a table and cup.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.23.5","WLC:Ps.23.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-084c1c2568d23edeb060","ref":"WLC:Ps.26.12","status":"accepted","reason":"The psalmist's foot stands on level ground and he blesses YHWH in the assembly in the same verse.","paragraphs":[58],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.26.12"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-008"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c530836b103150cdab49","ref":"WLC:Ps.37.24","status":"rejected","reason":"Established steps and delight in the way occur in Psalm 37:23; verse 24 instead says YHWH supports the falling person by the hand.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.37.24","WLC:Ps.37.23"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f7860f2de7a605074bcc","ref":"WLC:Ps.37.24","status":"rejected","reason":"YHWH holds up the one who falls, but Psalm 94:18 expresses the same support at the instant a foot slips, matching the page more closely.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.37.24"],"annotations":[]}
