+{"connection_id":"BC-97a8fd80fd2b6fb4ae48","ref":"WLC:Ps.91.12","status":"rejected","reason":"Angels carry a person to keep a foot from stone, but the text promises protection rather than help requested after faltering; Psalm 94:18 is closer.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.91.12"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-afad74ecd7773c5adb85","ref":"WLC:Ps.94.18","status":"accepted","reason":"The speaker says his foot slips and YHWH's steadfast love supports him; both danger and aid are explicit.","paragraphs":[58],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.94.18"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-009"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-be698cc71d02d78d8a8d","ref":"WLC:Ps.96.10","status":"rejected","reason":"Reign, stable world and equitable judgment share a verse, but this section's use of malik centers structural support and walking, not the judgment day.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.96.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-664261257275483a3bff","ref":"WLC:Ps.96.13","status":"rejected","reason":"The LORD comes to judge earth in righteousness, but this lacks the help and movement motif of paragraphs 55-58.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.96.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-77c87606dfac2aef830e","ref":"WLC:Zech.14.9","status":"rejected","reason":"YHWH becomes king over all the earth on that day; the verse does not speak of a judgment day or supporting a weak walker.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Zech.14.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1e84aced714528c024fd","ref":"WLC:Zeph.3.19","status":"rejected","reason":"God saves the lame and gathers the outcast in a restoration oracle, but no walking action or support is described.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Zeph.3.19"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a48e6e6087aac9eeb1a5","ref":"Wisdom 10:10","status":"unavailable","reason":"Wisdom 10:10 is absent from the local snapshot; its straight-path wording could not be checked.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Ps.27.11","status":"accepted","reason":"Independent original-language search and local commentary identify a direct prayer to be led on a level path.","paragraphs":[57],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.27.11"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-006"]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Ps.20.3","status":"rejected","reason":"The psalm requests help and support, but has no travel or upright-walking element beyond Isaiah 41:10's stronger hand imagery.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.20.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Ps.23.3","status":"rejected","reason":"The shepherd leads in righteous tracks, correcting the shifted Psalm 23:4 candidate, but Psalm 27:11 is the closer explicit petition.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.23.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:2Chr.14.10","status":"rejected","reason":"Asa's prayer asks God to help the powerless against the mighty; it corrects the 14:11 locator but is a military crisis with no road or gait.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:2Chr.14.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Ps.37.23","status":"rejected","reason":"The Lord establishes a person's steps, correcting the shifted Psalm 37:24 claim, but Psalm 94:18 more closely depicts a slip and support.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.37.23"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Ps.18.36","status":"rejected","reason":"The right hand supporting the singer appears here, correcting 2 Samuel 22:36, but the royal victory song adds no vulnerable traveler's plea.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.18.36"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Ps.17.5","status":"rejected","reason":"The speaker asks for held steps on God's tracks, but Psalm 27:11 has the straighter textual match and Psalm 94:18 the more concrete failed foot.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.17.5"],"annotations":[]}

